Faxbot: check the station that answers before any page, and stop waiting for a fax answer at 50 s (spandsp 0.0.6).

Two changes to a fax the built-in engine (res_fax_spandsp) sends, both off unless the dialplan marks the call.
The pure steps (faxbot_csi_check, faxbot_t0_ms, faxbot_t0_reached) are in faxbot_t38_gateway.h, with the reasons.

1. Station check (research N5). A phase B handler runs when the far end's DIS arrives. spandsp has already kept
   the far end's CSI by then, and it sends DCN before any DCS, training or page when the handler answers anything
   but T30_ERR_OK. With FAXBOT_CSI_EXPECT (the dialled number and the stations this number showed on earlier
   successful calls, digits separated by dots), a CSI that carries a full number that is none of them is a
   contradiction. A blank or short CSI is no signal. With FAXBOT_CSI_REFUSE=yes the call ends there as
   T30_ERR_IDENT_UNACCEPTABLE ("Far end's ident is not acceptable"); otherwise the fax goes on and Faxbot
   records that the station differed. FAXBOT_CSI_CHECK (matches, differs, refused or empty) goes on the channel
   at the end of the session for the dialplan's FaxResult event.

2. T0 cap. spandsp waits T0 = 60 s for the first fax message, and SendFAX starts only after answer, so a person
   who stays on the line costs a second billed minute on 60/60 billing. T.30 expects the machines to identify
   each other within T1 = 35 +-5 s once answered. With FAXBOT_T0_MS (40000 to 60000; Faxbot sets 50000 on trunk
   calls billed by the minute in steps of 60 s or more), a send session that has not reached phase B that long
   after the answer (FAXBOT_ANSWERED) is ended with t30_terminate, and FAXBOT_T0_CAPPED=1 goes on the channel. It
   counts from the answer, so a session res_fax starts again (T.38, or audio after a refused T.38 attempt) does not
   restart it.

Nothing here changes a call Faxbot did not mark, or a fax this engine receives.

